This repository incorporates adapted workflow and documentation concepts from
hw-eda-engineer, a skill package supplied by the project owner. Its supplied
SKILL.md declares license: MIT. No separate author or copyright notice was
provided in that package. Retain any original copyright and permission notices
if a separately obtained upstream distribution includes them.

The supplied scripts were reviewed; the connectivity checker in this repository
is a new implementation with a different, explicit input/coverage contract.
The later user-supplied hw-eda-engineer 0.5.0 package also declares MIT.
Its enclosure/project coordination, starter patterns, troubleshooting, worked
example, duty-cycle estimation and schematic geometry-review concepts informed
this update. The battery and schematic geometry helpers are new implementations
with explicit units, input validation and coverage limitations; the supplied
cost, project and Gerber checkers are not included as executable capabilities.
The original uploaded package is not included, including its environment-specific
output paths and fictional examples presented as real device pin mappings.

The later user-supplied hw-eda-engineer 0.6.0 package also declares MIT.
Its schematic/PCB lessons and before/after-module review approach informed
condition-scoped mechanism cards. Existing checks were retained and deduplicated;
universal component values, manufacturing claims, unverified sources and old
script contracts were not adopted as engineering guarantees.

